#
# Chapter 2 mostly states what a conformance claim is: documents, profiles
# and what applications may do. What a program or script can see of it is
# the presence of what the claim promises: the mandatory utilities, the
# utilities of each claimed option, the option constants that must go with
# an option group, and the length of external names in C. The constants
# that stand alone (_POSIX_VERSION, the always-defined options) are asserted
# in the <unistd.h> module.

assertion  XBD.2-conformance.001
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap02.html#2.1.3.2
anchor     functions/confstr.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       With PATH set to the value getconf PATH writes, each mandatory
           standard utility (those that need no option; the list is the one
           of the modules whose option is BASE, without localedef, which
           belongs to an option) is found by command -v.
note       Finding the name also succeeds for utilities built into the shell,
           which XCU 1.6 lets be missing from the path for the special and
           intrinsic utilities; whether each other utility can be reached
           through the exec functions is for the XCU 1.6 module.
test       t/001-mandatory-utilities.sh

assertion  XBD.2-conformance.002
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap02.html#2.1.6.2
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap02.html#2.1.1
class      required
since      1992
says       For each option of the shell and utilities that getconf reports as
           supported (a value above zero for POSIX2_C_DEV, POSIX2_FORT_RUN,
           POSIX2_LOCALEDEF, POSIX2_SW_DEV, POSIX2_UPE or XOPEN_UUCP), every
           utility listed for that option is found by command -v under the
           PATH from getconf PATH; NOTINUSE when no option is reported.
test       t/002-option-utilities.sh

assertion  XBD.2-conformance.003
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap02.html#2.1.4.2
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      2001
says       On an XSI system getconf reports POSIX2_UPE, POSIX2_CHAR_TERM and
           POSIX2_LOCALEDEF as defined and not -1, and the c17 utility is
           found by command -v.
test       t/003-xsi-shell-and-utilities.sh

assertion  XBD.2-conformance.004
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap02.html#2.1.4.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap02.html#2.1.5.2
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      2001
says       On an XSI system _POSIX_FSYNC, _POSIX_THREAD_ATTR_STACKADDR,
           _POSIX_THREAD_ATTR_STACKSIZE and _POSIX_THREAD_PROCESS_SHARED are
           defined by <unistd.h> with a value above zero (supported always).
test       t/004-xsi-options.c
nomutant   compile-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.2-conformance.005
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap02.html#2.1.5.2
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      2001
says       When _XOPEN_REALTIME is defined with a value other than -1,
           _POSIX_MEMLOCK, _POSIX_MEMLOCK_RANGE, _POSIX_MESSAGE_PASSING,
           _POSIX_PRIORITY_SCHEDULING, _POSIX_SHARED_MEMORY_OBJECTS and
           _POSIX_SYNCHRONIZED_IO are defined as 202405L; NOTINUSE when the
           Realtime Option Group is not claimed.
test       t/005-realtime-group.c
nomutant   compile-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.2-conformance.006
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap02.html#2.1.5.2
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      2001
says       When _XOPEN_REALTIME_THREADS is defined with a value other than -1,
           _POSIX_THREAD_PRIO_INHERIT, _POSIX_THREAD_PRIO_PROTECT,
           _POSIX_THREAD_PRIORITY_SCHEDULING,
           _POSIX_THREAD_ROBUST_PRIO_INHERIT and
           _POSIX_THREAD_ROBUST_PRIO_PROTECT are defined as 202405L; NOTINUSE
           when the Realtime Threads Option Group is not claimed.
test       t/006-realtime-threads-group.c
nomutant   compile-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.2-conformance.007
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap02.html#2.1.5.2
class      conditional
when       SS|TSP
since      2001
says       When _POSIX_SPORADIC_SERVER is defined as 202405L,
           _POSIX_PRIORITY_SCHEDULING is also defined as 202405L, and when
           _POSIX_THREAD_SPORADIC_SERVER is defined as 202405L,
           _POSIX_THREAD_PRIORITY_SCHEDULING is also defined as 202405L.
test       t/007-sporadic-needs-scheduling.c
nomutant   compile-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.2-conformance.008
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap02.html#2.4
class      conditional
when       CD
since      1992
says       The C implementation tells apart external names that differ in the
           31st byte, and external names that differ only in letter case:
           four such names defined in one C file and used from another link
           into a program that reads four different values.
note       The other-language wording of 2.4 applies to any language
           implementation that claims conformance; C is the only one the
           standard names.
test       t/008-external-names.sh
